pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* Regression test: a `spec` block after `transitivity`.
*
* Not a wrong verdict, and this too used to be ACCEPTED at exit 0. The order's
* specification is what its auxiliary variables mean, and `order_proof` pushes
* it as a premise of the transitivity and reflexivity proofs. Written after
* those proofs have run, it enters the order without ever having been a premise
* of the proofs that are supposed to hold under it -- so the order's side
* conditions were established for a different specification than the one
* `load_order` goes on to use. Found by the same sweep; see
* incorrect/version2/pre_order_transitivity_before_def.
f 4
pre_order simple
    vars
        left u1
        right v1
        aux
    end
    def
        -1 u1 1 v1 >= 0 ;
    end
    transitivity
        vars
            fresh_right w1
        end
        proof
            proofgoal #1
                p -2 -3 + -1 +
            end -1
        end
    end
    spec
    end
end
output NONE
conclusion NONE
end pseudo-Boolean proof
